1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,933
Sweetheart, my neighbor Agnes Whitfield was eighty-one

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:06,702
years old and worth about four million

3
00:00:06,702 --> 00:00:09,106
dollars, and not one of her three

4
00:00:09,106 --> 00:00:10,344
children knew it.

5
00:00:10,524 --> 00:00:12,619
So two weeks before Christmas,

6
00:00:12,619 --> 00:00:14,853
she called each of them with the

7
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:15,621
same story.

8
00:00:15,801 --> 00:00:18,518
She said, I've lost everything.

9
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:20,694
The bank's taking the house.

10
00:00:20,874 --> 00:00:22,732
Can I come live with you?

11
00:00:22,912 --> 00:00:25,208
And what each of those children said

12
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:27,377
back is the reason I'm telling you

13
00:00:27,377 --> 00:00:28,206
this tonight.

14
00:00:28,557 --> 00:00:31,120
Tonight I'll tell you what the oldest

15
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,199
said, what the middle one did,

16
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:34,724
and what the youngest,

17
00:00:34,724 --> 00:00:37,427
the one everybody called the failure of

18
00:00:37,427 --> 00:00:39,991
the family, showed up with at Agnes's

19
00:00:39,991 --> 00:00:41,862
door at two in the morning.

20
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:42,987
Stay with me,

21
00:00:42,987 --> 00:00:45,898
honey, because the reading of that will,

22
00:00:45,898 --> 00:00:46,843
a year later,

23
00:00:46,843 --> 00:00:50,117
was the most talked-about afternoon this town

24
00:00:50,117 --> 00:00:50,772
ever had.

25
00:00:51,122 --> 00:00:53,473
Agnes lived next door to me for

26
00:00:53,473 --> 00:00:54,838
thirty-four years.

27
00:00:55,018 --> 00:00:56,146
Her husband, Ed,

28
00:00:56,146 --> 00:00:58,965
had started a little trucking company in

29
00:00:58,965 --> 00:01:01,715
nineteen fifty-six with one truck and a

30
00:01:01,715 --> 00:01:02,843
borrowed dollar.

31
00:01:03,023 --> 00:01:04,487
By the time he died,

32
00:01:04,487 --> 00:01:06,390
he had two hundred trucks.

33
00:01:06,570 --> 00:01:09,375
But Ed and Agnes lived like they

34
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:10,076
had one.

35
00:01:10,256 --> 00:01:12,383
Same small brick house,

36
00:01:12,383 --> 00:01:15,527
same Chevrolet, same Sunday roast.

37
00:01:15,707 --> 00:01:18,074
They never told the children how much

38
00:01:18,074 --> 00:01:18,714
there was.

39
00:01:19,063 --> 00:01:20,122
Ed always said,

40
00:01:20,122 --> 00:01:23,298
money ruins children who know they're getting

41
00:01:23,298 --> 00:01:23,510
it.

42
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:25,977
Let them make their own way.

43
00:01:26,157 --> 00:01:28,582
So the three Whitfield children grew up

44
00:01:28,582 --> 00:01:31,068
thinking their parents were comfortable,

45
00:01:31,068 --> 00:01:32,125
and nothing more.

46
00:01:32,305 --> 00:01:35,358
Richard became a lawyer in Chicago.

47
00:01:35,538 --> 00:01:38,248
Diane married a dentist and moved to

48
00:01:38,248 --> 00:01:40,055
a big house in Columbus.

49
00:01:40,235 --> 00:01:41,655
And the youngest,

50
00:01:41,655 --> 00:01:45,080
Tommy, became a high school shop teacher,

51
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,084
right here in Mansfield.

52
00:01:47,435 --> 00:01:50,848
Richard and Diane were the success stories,

53
00:01:50,848 --> 00:01:51,324
honey.

54
00:01:51,504 --> 00:01:54,423
Agnes had their pictures on the mantel,

55
00:01:54,423 --> 00:01:55,695
in silver frames.

56
00:01:55,875 --> 00:01:59,451
Graduation, weddings, Christmas in Aspen.

57
00:01:59,631 --> 00:02:02,096
Tommy's picture was a school photo stuck

58
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:03,822
in the corner of the mirror.

59
00:02:04,002 --> 00:02:06,354
The other two talked about Tommy like

60
00:02:06,354 --> 00:02:07,880
he was a disappointment.

61
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,697
He never made any money.

62
00:02:09,877 --> 00:02:11,293
Married a waitress.

63
00:02:11,473 --> 00:02:13,698
Drove a pickup with a door that

64
00:02:13,698 --> 00:02:14,631
didn't match.

65
00:02:14,811 --> 00:02:16,799
In a minute I'll tell you why

66
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:18,375
that door didn't match.

67
00:02:18,726 --> 00:02:19,979
After Ed died,

68
00:02:19,979 --> 00:02:22,127
Agnes started to wonder.

69
00:02:22,307 --> 00:02:25,419
Her children called on birthdays and holidays.

70
00:02:25,599 --> 00:02:28,594
Richard and Diane sent beautiful gifts.

71
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:30,202
But they never came.

72
00:02:30,382 --> 00:02:32,669
Not once in three years.

73
00:02:32,849 --> 00:02:34,554
And Agnes said to me,

74
00:02:34,554 --> 00:02:37,151
over coffee at my kitchen table,

75
00:02:37,151 --> 00:02:39,667
Ruth, I have to decide who gets

76
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:41,371
four million dollars.

77
00:02:41,551 --> 00:02:43,613
And I don't know my own children

78
00:02:43,613 --> 00:02:44,128
anymore.

79
00:02:44,308 --> 00:02:46,421
I know their Christmas cards.

80
00:02:46,772 --> 00:02:48,478
So she made her plan,

81
00:02:48,478 --> 00:02:50,185
and she told only me,

82
00:02:50,185 --> 00:02:52,542
because she needed a witness.

83
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:55,224
She'd call each child and tell them

84
00:02:55,224 --> 00:02:57,584
that Ed's company had gone under,

85
00:02:57,584 --> 00:03:00,301
the bank was foreclosing on the house,

86
00:03:00,301 --> 00:03:02,161
and she had nowhere to go.

87
00:03:02,341 --> 00:03:04,472
She'd ask each one if she could

88
00:03:04,472 --> 00:03:05,847
come live with them.

89
00:03:06,027 --> 00:03:08,504
And she'd keep a little notebook of

90
00:03:08,504 --> 00:03:10,415
exactly what each one said.

91
00:03:10,766 --> 00:03:12,843
I told her it was cruel,

92
00:03:12,843 --> 00:03:13,796
sweetheart.

93
00:03:13,976 --> 00:03:15,195
I said, Agnes,

94
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,459
you'll break their hearts.

95
00:03:17,639 --> 00:03:19,814
And she looked at me and said,

96
00:03:19,814 --> 00:03:22,134
Ruth, if it breaks their hearts,

97
00:03:22,134 --> 00:03:24,454
then I'll know they have hearts.

98
00:03:24,634 --> 00:03:26,889
Then I'll tell them the truth and

99
00:03:26,889 --> 00:03:28,803
we'll all have a good cry at

100
00:03:28,803 --> 00:03:29,487
Christmas.

101
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:31,014
That's all I want.

102
00:03:31,194 --> 00:03:32,958
I want to find out they have

103
00:03:32,958 --> 00:03:33,399
hearts.

104
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:36,468
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

105
00:03:36,468 --> 00:03:38,566
tap the like button for me,

106
00:03:38,566 --> 00:03:39,032
honey.

107
00:03:39,212 --> 00:03:42,451
It helps more people find these stories.

108
00:03:42,631 --> 00:03:44,643
She called Richard first,

109
00:03:44,643 --> 00:03:46,172
on a Tuesday night.

110
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:48,163
I sat next to her on the

111
00:03:48,163 --> 00:03:48,616
couch.

112
00:03:48,796 --> 00:03:50,224
Richard listened.

113
00:03:50,404 --> 00:03:52,308
There was a long pause.

114
00:03:52,488 --> 00:03:54,067
And then he said,

115
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,018
Mom, that's terrible.

116
00:03:56,198 --> 00:03:58,113
Have you talked to a lawyer?

117
00:03:58,293 --> 00:03:59,300
And she said,

118
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,080
honey, you're a lawyer.

119
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:02,285
And he said,

120
00:04:02,285 --> 00:04:04,761
well, I don't do that kind of

121
00:04:04,761 --> 00:04:05,103
law.

122
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,891
Then she asked him straight out.

123
00:04:08,071 --> 00:04:10,631
Richard, can I come stay with you

124
00:04:10,631 --> 00:04:11,484
and Pamela?

125
00:04:11,664 --> 00:04:14,253
Just until I get on my feet?

126
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:16,360
Another long pause.

127
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:17,983
Then Richard said,

128
00:04:17,983 --> 00:04:20,627
Mom, you know our place is small.

129
00:04:20,807 --> 00:04:23,272
And Pamela's mother is coming for the

130
00:04:23,272 --> 00:04:23,872
holidays.

131
00:04:24,052 --> 00:04:27,024
Have you looked into those senior apartments?

132
00:04:27,204 --> 00:04:29,480
I could help with the first month.

133
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:32,863
Richard lived in a five-bedroom house in

134
00:04:32,863 --> 00:04:34,385
Lake Forest, honey.

135
00:04:34,735 --> 00:04:37,091
Agnes thanked him and hung up.

136
00:04:37,271 --> 00:04:39,547
She wrote in her little notebook.

137
00:04:39,727 --> 00:04:40,528
Richard.

138
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:42,090
Senior apartment.

139
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:43,384
First month.

140
00:04:43,564 --> 00:04:46,054
Then she sat there with that notebook

141
00:04:46,054 --> 00:04:47,871
on her lap for a long time.

142
00:04:48,051 --> 00:04:50,073
And I didn't say anything,

143
00:04:50,073 --> 00:04:52,951
because there wasn't anything to say.

144
00:04:53,131 --> 00:04:55,929
She'd been his mother for fifty-six years,

145
00:04:55,929 --> 00:04:58,460
and he'd offered her one month's rent.

146
00:04:58,810 --> 00:05:00,957
She called Diane the next night.

147
00:05:01,137 --> 00:05:03,529
Diane cried, honey.

148
00:05:03,709 --> 00:05:06,305
Real tears, I could hear them through

149
00:05:06,305 --> 00:05:07,006
the phone.

150
00:05:07,186 --> 00:05:08,472
She said, oh,

151
00:05:08,472 --> 00:05:09,659
Mama, oh no.

152
00:05:09,839 --> 00:05:11,337
And for a minute,

153
00:05:11,337 --> 00:05:13,276
I thought, here it is.

154
00:05:13,456 --> 00:05:14,756
Here's the heart.

155
00:05:14,936 --> 00:05:16,199
Then Diane said,

156
00:05:16,199 --> 00:05:19,278
Mama, what happened to Daddy's company?

157
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:21,211
Was there anything left?

158
00:05:21,391 --> 00:05:23,481
What about the house in Florida?

159
00:05:23,661 --> 00:05:24,996
What about the jewelry?

160
00:05:25,176 --> 00:05:28,358
Is Grandma's ring still in the safe

161
00:05:28,358 --> 00:05:29,449
deposit box?

162
00:05:29,799 --> 00:05:32,399
When Agnes asked if she could come

163
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,470
live with her,

164
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:34,770
Diane said, Mama,

165
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:37,217
you know I would in a heartbeat.

166
00:05:37,397 --> 00:05:39,269
But Greg has his practice,

167
00:05:39,269 --> 00:05:41,860
and the girls have their activities,

168
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:44,236
and we're redoing the guest room.

169
00:05:44,416 --> 00:05:46,122
Let me talk to Greg.

170
00:05:46,302 --> 00:05:47,765
I'll call you back.

171
00:05:47,945 --> 00:05:50,383
Agnes wrote in her notebook.

172
00:05:50,563 --> 00:05:51,527
Diane.

173
00:05:51,707 --> 00:05:53,413
Asked about the ring.

174
00:05:53,593 --> 00:05:54,975
Will call back.

175
00:05:55,155 --> 00:05:57,161
Diane never called back,

176
00:05:57,161 --> 00:05:58,081
sweetheart.

177
00:05:58,261 --> 00:05:59,468
Not that week.

178
00:05:59,648 --> 00:06:00,740
Not ever.

179
00:06:01,090 --> 00:06:03,446
She almost didn't call Tommy.

180
00:06:03,626 --> 00:06:04,986
She said, Ruth,

181
00:06:04,986 --> 00:06:06,889
he doesn't have room.

182
00:06:07,069 --> 00:06:09,746
He's got three kids in a two-bedroom

183
00:06:09,746 --> 00:06:10,192
house.

184
00:06:10,372 --> 00:06:12,566
It isn't fair to ask him.

185
00:06:12,746 --> 00:06:13,725
But I said,

186
00:06:13,725 --> 00:06:16,485
Agnes, you asked the other two.

187
00:06:16,665 --> 00:06:18,288
So on Thursday night,

188
00:06:18,288 --> 00:06:19,602
she called Tommy.

189
00:06:19,782 --> 00:06:22,382
And she told him the same story.

190
00:06:22,562 --> 00:06:24,374
The company, the bank,

191
00:06:24,374 --> 00:06:25,198
the house.

192
00:06:25,378 --> 00:06:27,479
And she hadn't even gotten to the

193
00:06:27,479 --> 00:06:29,325
question when he cut her off.

194
00:06:29,676 --> 00:06:30,996
He said, Mom,

195
00:06:30,996 --> 00:06:33,333
are you safe right now?

196
00:06:33,513 --> 00:06:34,767
Are you warm?

197
00:06:34,947 --> 00:06:36,885
Is there food in the house?

198
00:06:37,065 --> 00:06:38,718
She said, yes,

199
00:06:38,718 --> 00:06:40,606
honey, I'm fine.

200
00:06:40,786 --> 00:06:42,319
And he said,

201
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:42,958
okay.

202
00:06:43,138 --> 00:06:44,554
Don't do anything.

203
00:06:44,734 --> 00:06:46,406
Don't sign anything.

204
00:06:46,586 --> 00:06:47,549
I'm coming.

205
00:06:47,729 --> 00:06:49,053
And he hung up.

206
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:51,759
Agnes looked at me and said,

207
00:06:51,759 --> 00:06:52,391
coming?

208
00:06:52,571 --> 00:06:54,266
It's ten o'clock at night.

209
00:06:54,446 --> 00:06:55,536
I said, Agnes,

210
00:06:55,536 --> 00:06:57,870
I think your son is getting in

211
00:06:57,870 --> 00:06:58,649
his truck.

212
00:06:58,999 --> 00:07:01,190
At two o'clock in the morning,

213
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:04,258
there were headlights in Agnes's driveway.

214
00:07:04,438 --> 00:07:07,329
I saw them from my bedroom window.

215
00:07:07,509 --> 00:07:09,427
It was Tommy's old pickup,

216
00:07:09,427 --> 00:07:11,861
the one with the door that didn't

217
00:07:11,861 --> 00:07:12,304
match.

218
00:07:12,484 --> 00:07:13,771
And in the back,

219
00:07:13,771 --> 00:07:15,782
under a tarp in the snow,

220
00:07:15,782 --> 00:07:17,391
was a twin mattress,

221
00:07:17,391 --> 00:07:18,920
a box of groceries,

222
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,127
a space heater,

223
00:07:20,127 --> 00:07:21,656
and a set of tools.

224
00:07:21,836 --> 00:07:24,080
He'd driven over from the other side

225
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,449
of town with everything he thought his

226
00:07:26,449 --> 00:07:27,571
mother might need.

227
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:30,568
Agnes opened the door in her robe.

228
00:07:30,748 --> 00:07:33,251
And Tommy, her disappointment,

229
00:07:33,251 --> 00:07:36,755
the shop teacher with the mismatched door,

230
00:07:36,755 --> 00:07:39,258
said, Mom, Carla and I talked.

231
00:07:39,438 --> 00:07:41,237
The kids are going to double up.

232
00:07:41,417 --> 00:07:43,403
You're getting Katie's room.

233
00:07:43,583 --> 00:07:45,231
It's got the best light.

234
00:07:45,411 --> 00:07:47,478
We'll get your things tomorrow.

235
00:07:47,658 --> 00:07:50,125
And if the bank wants this house,

236
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:51,396
they can have it.

237
00:07:51,576 --> 00:07:52,888
You've got us.

238
00:07:53,068 --> 00:07:54,926
You've always got us.

239
00:07:55,276 --> 00:07:56,831
Agnes asked him,

240
00:07:56,831 --> 00:07:59,165
honey, what about money?

241
00:07:59,345 --> 00:08:00,355
Tommy laughed.

242
00:08:00,535 --> 00:08:01,747
He said, Mom,

243
00:08:01,747 --> 00:08:03,426
we don't have any.

244
00:08:03,606 --> 00:08:05,057
We never have.

245
00:08:05,237 --> 00:08:06,793
We'll figure it out.

246
00:08:06,973 --> 00:08:08,691
We always do.

247
00:08:08,871 --> 00:08:10,732
And then he told her about the

248
00:08:10,732 --> 00:08:11,042
door.

249
00:08:11,222 --> 00:08:14,480
The pickup's passenger door was green because

250
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,941
he'd bought it at a junkyard after

251
00:08:16,941 --> 00:08:18,606
a drunk driver hit him.

252
00:08:18,786 --> 00:08:21,198
He'd been driving it two years,

253
00:08:21,198 --> 00:08:23,454
because new doors cost money,

254
00:08:23,454 --> 00:08:25,555
and his kids needed braces.

255
00:08:25,904 --> 00:08:28,294
Agnes broke down right there in the

256
00:08:28,294 --> 00:08:29,318
hallway, honey.

257
00:08:29,498 --> 00:08:31,321
She told him everything.

258
00:08:31,501 --> 00:08:33,364
The test, the notebook,

259
00:08:33,364 --> 00:08:35,390
the four million dollars.

260
00:08:35,570 --> 00:08:37,118
And Tommy stood there,

261
00:08:37,118 --> 00:08:39,370
and his face went from confused,

262
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:42,397
to hurt, to something I've never forgotten.

263
00:08:42,577 --> 00:08:43,671
He said, Mom,

264
00:08:43,671 --> 00:08:45,943
you didn't have to test me.

265
00:08:46,123 --> 00:08:47,844
You just had to ask me to

266
00:08:47,844 --> 00:08:49,014
Christmas dinner.

267
00:08:49,194 --> 00:08:51,643
And then he went outside and sat

268
00:08:51,643 --> 00:08:53,862
in his truck for a long time.

269
00:08:54,211 --> 00:08:55,638
So far, the lawyer,

270
00:08:55,638 --> 00:08:57,891
the ring, and the truck at two

271
00:08:57,891 --> 00:08:59,018
in the morning.

272
00:08:59,198 --> 00:09:02,415
Agnes spent that Christmas at Tommy's little

273
00:09:02,415 --> 00:09:05,048
house, in Katie's room with the best

274
00:09:05,048 --> 00:09:07,827
light, eating Carla's ham on a folding

275
00:09:07,827 --> 00:09:08,265
chair.

276
00:09:08,445 --> 00:09:10,804
She told me it was the happiest

277
00:09:10,804 --> 00:09:13,391
Christmas she'd had since Ed died.

278
00:09:13,571 --> 00:09:15,893
Richard sent a fruit basket.

279
00:09:16,073 --> 00:09:18,221
Diane sent a card that asked if

280
00:09:18,221 --> 00:09:20,299
there was news about the ring.

281
00:09:20,649 --> 00:09:23,945
Agnes never told Richard and Diane the

282
00:09:23,945 --> 00:09:25,073
truth, honey.

283
00:09:25,253 --> 00:09:27,104
Not that Christmas,

284
00:09:27,104 --> 00:09:27,981
not ever.

285
00:09:28,161 --> 00:09:29,280
She said, Ruth,

286
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,668
they had their chance to show me

287
00:09:31,668 --> 00:09:32,712
who they were.

288
00:09:32,892 --> 00:09:34,731
I'm not going to give them a

289
00:09:34,731 --> 00:09:37,554
second one with the answers already written

290
00:09:37,554 --> 00:09:38,407
on the board.

291
00:09:38,587 --> 00:09:41,364
She paid off Tommy's house that January,

292
00:09:41,364 --> 00:09:43,169
and told him it was from a

293
00:09:43,169 --> 00:09:45,599
little savings account Ed had left.

294
00:09:45,779 --> 00:09:47,567
She bought the kids braces.

295
00:09:47,747 --> 00:09:49,187
She bought him a new door.

296
00:09:49,537 --> 00:09:51,979
Agnes passed the next December,

297
00:09:51,979 --> 00:09:53,948
peacefully, in her sleep,

298
00:09:53,948 --> 00:09:56,469
in the room with the best light.

299
00:09:56,649 --> 00:09:57,704
And in January,

300
00:09:57,704 --> 00:10:00,236
all three children sat in a lawyer's

301
00:10:00,236 --> 00:10:02,697
office for the reading of the will.

302
00:10:02,877 --> 00:10:05,309
Richard flew in from Chicago in a

303
00:10:05,309 --> 00:10:06,488
long black coat.

304
00:10:06,668 --> 00:10:08,711
Diane came in a fur.

305
00:10:08,891 --> 00:10:11,260
Tommy came in his work boots.

306
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,936
I was there too,

307
00:10:12,936 --> 00:10:16,303
honey, because Agnes had asked me to

308
00:10:16,303 --> 00:10:16,583
be.

309
00:10:16,933 --> 00:10:19,023
The lawyer read it slowly.

310
00:10:19,203 --> 00:10:20,570
To my son Richard,

311
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:22,772
I leave one month's rent at a

312
00:10:22,772 --> 00:10:25,277
senior apartment of his choosing,

313
00:10:25,277 --> 00:10:27,783
so he'll know what it feels like.

314
00:10:27,963 --> 00:10:29,469
To my daughter Diane,

315
00:10:29,469 --> 00:10:31,261
I leave my mother's ring,

316
00:10:31,261 --> 00:10:33,698
since that's what she asked about.

317
00:10:33,878 --> 00:10:35,178
To my son Thomas,

318
00:10:35,178 --> 00:10:37,547
who came at two in the morning,

319
00:10:37,547 --> 00:10:39,381
I leave everything else.

320
00:10:39,561 --> 00:10:41,442
And then he said the number.

321
00:10:41,622 --> 00:10:44,734
Four million, one hundred thousand dollars.

322
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:46,906
Diane screamed.

323
00:10:47,086 --> 00:10:49,174
Richard said he'd contest it,

324
00:10:49,174 --> 00:10:51,766
and then he saw the little notebook,

325
00:10:51,766 --> 00:10:54,215
which the lawyer pulled out of the

326
00:10:54,215 --> 00:10:57,239
folder, with every phone call written down

327
00:10:57,239 --> 00:11:00,263
in Agnes's handwriting and my signature as

328
00:11:00,263 --> 00:11:02,783
witness at the bottom of each page.

329
00:11:02,963 --> 00:11:04,778
He didn't contest it,

330
00:11:04,778 --> 00:11:05,297
honey.

331
00:11:05,477 --> 00:11:06,487
And Tommy?

332
00:11:06,667 --> 00:11:09,216
Tommy just sat there with his hands

333
00:11:09,216 --> 00:11:10,891
on his knees and cried,

334
00:11:10,891 --> 00:11:13,512
because all he wanted was his mother

335
00:11:13,512 --> 00:11:13,876
back.

336
00:11:14,226 --> 00:11:16,909
Tommy still teaches shop at the high

337
00:11:16,909 --> 00:11:18,325
school, sweetheart.

338
00:11:18,505 --> 00:11:20,002
He didn't quit.

339
00:11:20,182 --> 00:11:22,412
He still drives a pickup.

340
00:11:22,592 --> 00:11:24,136
But every Christmas Eve,

341
00:11:24,136 --> 00:11:26,325
he takes the families of every one

342
00:11:26,325 --> 00:11:28,448
of his students who's struggling,

343
00:11:28,448 --> 00:11:30,959
and he quietly pays their heating bills

344
00:11:30,959 --> 00:11:32,181
through the winter.

345
00:11:32,361 --> 00:11:34,184
He calls it the two a.

346
00:11:34,364 --> 00:11:35,026
m.

347
00:11:35,206 --> 00:11:35,856
fund.

348
00:11:36,036 --> 00:11:37,615
Nobody knows it's him.

349
00:11:37,795 --> 00:11:39,189
Nobody but me,

350
00:11:39,189 --> 00:11:40,384
and now you.

351
00:11:40,734 --> 00:11:43,628
Here's what I want you to remember,

352
00:11:43,628 --> 00:11:44,125
honey.

353
00:11:44,305 --> 00:11:46,777
You never know who your real riches

354
00:11:46,777 --> 00:11:48,473
are until you need them.

355
00:11:48,653 --> 00:11:51,046
Agnes had a mantel full of silver

356
00:11:51,046 --> 00:11:53,658
frames and one school photo stuck in

357
00:11:53,658 --> 00:11:56,124
the mirror, and she had it exactly

358
00:11:56,124 --> 00:11:56,849
backwards.

359
00:11:57,029 --> 00:11:59,034
Call the one who'd come at two

360
00:11:59,034 --> 00:12:00,036
in the morning.

361
00:12:00,216 --> 00:12:02,518
And if you're the one who would,

362
00:12:02,518 --> 00:12:03,525
God bless you.

363
00:12:03,705 --> 00:12:05,168
Don't ever stop.

364
00:12:05,517 --> 00:12:07,412
Tell me in the comments,

365
00:12:07,412 --> 00:12:08,281
sweetheart.

366
00:12:08,461 --> 00:12:11,224
Was Agnes right to test her children,

367
00:12:11,224 --> 00:12:12,420
or was it wrong?

368
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,585
And who in your family would come

369
00:12:14,585 --> 00:12:15,908
at two in the morning?

370
00:12:16,088 --> 00:12:18,424
There are more of my family's stories

371
00:12:18,424 --> 00:12:20,634
in the playlist right there on your

372
00:12:20,634 --> 00:12:22,591
screen, and I'll see you in the

373
00:12:22,591 --> 00:12:23,159
next one.

374
00:12:23,339 --> 00:12:24,953
Good night, honey.
